{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And showing kindness to thousands, etc.</b> The meaning is that even one who performs acts of kindness — the Holy One, blessed be He, does not repay him for all his kindness immediately and at once, but rather selects for him a fitting manner of repayment across the generations, and goes on paying in every generation that needs it. And it contains a quality that establishes protection and deliverance up to thousands. This is what our Sages of blessed memory said (Exodus Rabbah 44:3) — that if the Holy One, blessed be He, were to repay the patriarchs their reward in this world, with what would their children be sustained in every generation and in the exiles?" "And its saying <b>and to those who keep My commandments</b> — our Sages of blessed memory explained (Sotah 31a) that it does not connect with \"to thousands,\" for those who serve out of fear, if the generations should need his merit, it will not extend beyond a thousand, as is explicitly stated in another verse, where it is written (Deuteronomy 7:9) ״לְאֶלֶף דּוֹר״ (\"to a thousand generations\"), etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:30:46.887568882Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}